    {
      "paperId": "/chapter/10.1007/978-1-4614-8130-0_3",
      "doi": "10.1007/978-1-4614-8130-0_3",
      "title": "Optical Properties of Lateral InGaAs Quantum Dot Molecules Single- and Bi-Layers",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "Songphol Kanjanachuchai, Nirat Patanasemakul, ... Somsak Panyakeow"
        }
      ],
      "year": 2014,
      "abstract": "Growth of InGaAs nanostructures by molecular beam epitaxy using partial-cap and regrowth technique results in an ensemble of lateral quantum dot molecules (QDMs). Each QDM comprises a large, central quantum dot and several small, satellite quantum dots which emit at different energies and exhibit qualitatively different optical behaviors. This chapter reviews, explains, and discusses the various fundamental aspects of lateral QDM single layers: the nucleation mechanism, the photoluminescent spectra, and the unique bimodal optical characteristics. The chapter ends by demonstrating the usefulness of lateral QDM bi-layers as a promising broadband near-infrared material.",
